---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import { url } from '../../site';

const updated = '26 October 2026';
const repo = 'https://github.com/Geodude117/Wee-Alarm';
---

<Base
  title="Wee Alarm privacy policy"
  description="Privacy policy for the Wee Alarm iPhone app. The app doesn't collect any personal data."
>
  <p class="eyebrow"><a href={url('wee-alarm/')}>Wee Alarm</a></p>
  <h1>Privacy policy</h1>
  <p class="muted">Last updated {updated}</p>

  <div class="prose">
    <p class="summary">
      <strong>In short:</strong> Wee Alarm doesn't collect, store or share any personal data. Your dog's details and
      alarm times stay on your iPhone.
    </p>

    <h2>Who we are</h2>
    <p>
      Wee Alarm is made by Geovan, an independent developer based in the United Kingdom. This policy covers the Wee
      Alarm app for iPhone.
    </p>

    <h2>Information the app collects</h2>
    <p>None. Wee Alarm:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>has no accounts, sign-in or registration;</li>
      <li>doesn't ask for your name, email address, location, contacts, photos, camera or microphone;</li>
      <li>has no advertising, analytics, crash-reporting or tracking of any kind;</li>
      <li>doesn't include any third-party software that collects data;</li>
      <li>doesn't send anything over the internet, so nothing is sent to us or anyone else.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Information stored on your device</h2>
    <p>To work, the app saves a few details on your iPhone using the standard iOS settings storage:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>your dog's name, age group (puppy, adult or senior) and size;</li>
      <li>how often you want a wee-break reminder, and your quiet hours;</li>
      <li>when you last let your dog out, and whether you've snoozed the reminder.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      This information never leaves your device and we can't see it. It's deleted when you tap <em>Start over</em> in
      the app's settings or delete the app. If you use iCloud or device backups, it may be included in your own backup,
      under Apple's privacy policy.
    </p>

    <h2>Alarms and notifications</h2>
    <p>
      With your permission, Wee Alarm asks iOS to set an alarm (or, if alarms are turned off, a notification) for your
      next wee break. The alarm shows your dog's name, for example "Biscuit needs a wee". iOS schedules and shows the
      alarm on your device, and may also show it on a paired Apple Watch. None of this is sent to us. You can turn alarms
      and notifications off at any time in the iOS Settings app.
    </p>

    <h2>Links to this website</h2>
    <p>
      The app's settings include links to this privacy policy and the support page, which open in your web browser. This
      website is hosted by GitHub Pages. GitHub may log technical information such as your IP address when you visit,
      as described in the
      <a href="https://docs.github.com/en/site-policy/privacy-policies/github-general-privacy-statement" rel="noopener" target="_blank">GitHub privacy statement</a>.
      We don't use cookies or analytics on this site.
    </p>

    <h2>Children</h2>
    <p>
      Wee Alarm is a general-audience app and isn't directed at children. Because it doesn't collect any personal data,
      it doesn't collect data from children. It has no in-app purchases, advertising, chat or sharing features.
    </p>

    <h2>Your rights</h2>
    <p>
      Under UK data protection law you have rights over personal data that organisations hold about you. As Wee Alarm
      doesn't collect any personal data, we don't hold any data about you. You can remove everything the app has saved
      on your device by tapping <em>Start over</em> or deleting the app.
    </p>

    <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
    <p>
      If the app ever changes in a way that affects your privacy, this page will be updated before that version is
      released, and the date at the top will change.
    </p>

    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>
      Questions about this policy? Please
      <a href={`${repo}/issues/new`} rel="noopener" target="_blank">open an issue on GitHub</a> or see the
      <a href={url('wee-alarm/#support')}>Wee Alarm support page</a>.
    </p>
  </div>
</Base>

<style>
  .summary {
    padding: 1rem 1.25rem;
    border-radius: var(--radius);
    background: var(--accent-soft);
  }
</style>
